(12153, 3847, 'Beginner - I do not know what a subquery is.', 10, 1, TRUE, NULL, NULL, TRUE, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'To achieve this level of understanding, the user should start by learning the basics of SQL and then move on to understanding the concept of subqueries. They should practice writing subqueries and understand how they can be used to retrieve data from multiple tables. The user should also learn about the different types of subqueries and how they can be used in different scenarios.', 'To achieve this level of understanding, the user should start by learning the basics of SQL and then move on to understanding the concept of subqueries. They should practice writing subqueries and understand how they can be used to retrieve data from multiple tables. The user should also learn about the different types of subqueries and how they can be used in different scenarios.', 0),
