(12157, 3847, 'Expert - I can implement subquery strategies.', 50, 5, NULL, NULL, TRUE, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'To achieve this level of understanding, the user should have a deep understanding of SQL and should have extensive experience writing subqueries. They should be able to write complex subqueries to retrieve data from multiple tables and should be familiar with the different types of subqueries. The user should also be able to use subqueries in different scenarios and understand their limitations.In addition, the user should be able to optimize subqueries for performance and understand how to use subqueries in conjunction with other SQL concepts such as joins and aggregates.', 'To achieve this level of understanding, the user should have a deep understanding of SQL and should have extensive experience writing subqueries. They should be able to write complex subqueries to retrieve data from multiple tables and should be familiar with the different types of subqueries. The user should also be able to use subqueries in different scenarios and understand their limitations. In addition, the user should be able to optimize subqueries for performance and understand how to use subqueries in conjunction with other SQL concepts such as joins and aggregates.', NULL),
(12158, 3848, 'Beginner - I do not know what a stored procedure is.', 10, 1, TRUE, NULL, NULL, TRUE, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'To achieve this level, you need to start by learning the basics of SQL and database management. You can start by taking online courses or reading books on the subject. Once you have a good understanding of SQL, you can start learning about stored procedures and how they work. Practice writing simple stored procedures and gradually work your way up to more complex ones. With time and practice, you will become comfortable with stored procedures and be able to use them effectively in your work.', 'To achieve this level, you need to learn the basics of SQL and database management. Start by taking online courses or reading books on the subject. Once you have a good understanding of SQL, start learning about stored procedures and how they work. Practice writing simple stored procedures and gradually work your way up to more complex ones. With time and practice, you will become comfortable with stored procedures and be able to use them effectively in your work.', 0),
(12159, 3848, 'Elementary - I have heard of stored procedures but have never used them.', 20, 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'To achieve this level, you need to start by learning the basics of SQL and database management. You can start by taking online courses or reading books on the subject. Once you have a good understanding of SQL, you can start learning about stored procedures and how they work. Practice writing simple stored procedures and gradually work your way up to more complex ones. With time and practice, you will become comfortable with stored procedures and be able to use them effectively in your work.', 'To achieve this level, you need to learn the basics of SQL and database management. Start by taking online courses or reading books on the subject. Once you have a good understanding of SQL, start learning about stored procedures and how they work. Practice writing simple stored procedures and gradually work your way up to more complex ones. With time and practice, you will become comfortable with stored procedures and be able to use them effectively in your work.', NULL),
